Time Complexity: For insert operation: O(1) (As insertion 'push' in a stack takes constant time)For delete operation: O(1) (As deletion 'pop' in a stack takes constant time)For 'Get Min' operation: O(1) (As we have used an auxiliary stack which has it's top as the minimum element)Auxiliary Space: O(n)Using a Pair in Stack - O(1) Time and O(n) SpaceThis approach uses a stack where each element is stored as a pair: the element itself and the minimum value up to that point. When an element is pushed, the minimum is updated. The getMin() function directly accesses the minimum value from the top of the stack in constant time, ensuring that both push(), pop(), and getMin() operations are O(1). This approach efficiently tracks the minimum value without needing to traverse the stack.
